# web2mp3 application configuration.
# Copy this file to `.config/.env` and fill in the real values
# (or, when running via Docker, let docker-compose bind-mount your own
# ./.config/.env here).
#
# Fill in every value below (MUSIC_DIR, SPOTIPY_CLIENT_ID,
# SPOTIPY_CLIENT_SECRET, LOCATION) before first run and web2mp3 will skip
# its interactive setup wizard entirely — it only runs if one of these four
# is still missing. The one interactive step that's unavoidable on first run
# is the Spotify OAuth login itself (a browser authorization), since that
# needs a live login rather than a config value.

# Fixed internal path when running via Docker — the music library itself
# is bind-mounted to /music by docker-compose (see .env.example at the repo
# root for the real host path). Leave this as /music for Docker use.
MUSIC_DIR=/music

# Spotify Developer credentials: https://developer.spotify.com/dashboard
SPOTIPY_CLIENT_ID=
SPOTIPY_CLIENT_SECRET=

# Spotify API market / your country code, e.g. NL, US.
LOCATION=US

# Optional: path to a Netscape-format cookies.txt for age-restricted YouTube
# downloads. If omitted, any *_cookies.txt placed in this ./.config
# directory is auto-detected.
# COOKIE_FILE=/app/.config/cookies.txt
